    "description": "Lot of 3 Art Prints Ming Dynasty Dragon Pipe Bowl and Decorative Patterns\nThis lot includes three art prints featuring historical and cultural designs. The first print depicts a detailed dragon motif from the Ming Dynasty, sourced from the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York, representing Chinese Ming Dynasty embroidery or textile art. The second print shows a stone pipe bowl carved as a human head, attributed to an anonymous artist and part of the National Museums of Scotland collection, photographed against a blue background. The third print is a black-and-white sheet with various intricate decorative patterns arranged in a grid, likely architectural or textile motifs. All prints are on glossy paper and are in good condition with minor creasing at the edges.\nProduct Size:\n23 x 18 x 1 in\n1 lb",
